Do not take other tones in the button window of a DFT pen for a button (ButtonToneRatio)

Without a decision from the MPP v2 binary window the button state comes from the first row of
the button window: a magnitude above ButtonMinMag counts as a pressed button or an eraser. The
following rows of that window carry other tones of the pen, and what they leak into the first row
passes that threshold. Measured on the Surface Pro 9 with the Slim Pen 2 (no button pressed):
405 of 3529 button windows of one capture, 128 of 1636 of another and all 999 of a third (pen
resting at 37 degrees). In every one of them the strongest of the rows 1 to 3 had more than 10
times the magnitude of row 0, on both axes.

With [DFT] ButtonToneRatio = N the first row is not a button while, on both axes, one of the
rows 1 to 3 is more than N times stronger. With 3 none of these windows counts any more. The
decision of the binary window and the two-frame debounce are unchanged. Off by default (0).

Not tested with the button pressed: that a genuine button tone is not accompanied by much
stronger tones in the next rows is an assumption, which is why both axes have to agree and the
ratio is far below what was measured.

